    <DataNode elementId="AT4G33520-MONOMER" textLabel="Copper-transporting ATPase PAA1, chloroplastic" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9SZC9" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="215" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pujar, O-28, caspi, SRI, pmngroup">Copper is an essential nutrient for electron transport processes, but also very toxic when present in excess, necessitating precise delivery systems. The chloroplast is a major sink for Cu in plants because Cu is an important cofactor for the photosynthetic electron transport. |FRAME: Plastocyanins Plastocyanin|, a blue copper protein that is one of the most abundant proteins in the thylakoid lumen, catalyzes electron transfer between the |FRAME: CPLX490-29 cytochrome &lt;i&gt;b&lt;/i&gt;&lt;sub&gt;6&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;i&gt;f&lt;/i&gt; complex| and |FRAME:CPLX-985 photosystem I|. A cDNA clone was isolated from |FRAME: TAX-3702 &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt;| and found to encode a metal transporting P type ATPase. The gene was named |FRAME: G-11069 PAA1| (P-type ATPase of Arabidopsis), and was the first metal transporting ATPase isolated and characterized from higher plants |CITS: [9188794]|. In subsequent work the protein was found to be a critical component of a Cu transport system in chloroplasts |CITS: [12782727]|. The exact nature of the protein was understood after a related protein,|FRAME: G-11070 PAA2|, has also been characterized. Although both |FRAME: G-11069 PAA1| and |FRAME: G-11070 PAA2| are localized in the chloroplast, they are found in different sub-cellular locations and work in tandem. |FRAME: G-11069 PAA1| is located in the chloroplast membrane and transport |FRAME: CU+2 Cu&lt;SUP&gt;2+&lt;/SUP&gt;| from the cytoplasm into the chloroplast stroma, while |FRAME: G-11070 PAA2| is located in the thylakoid membranes and transports the copper from the stroma into the thylakoid |CITS: [15772282]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT4G33520-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT4G33520.2" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q9SZC9" />
